# How to configure a cluster based application for ov_mc_vocs

A cluster based application is automatically forwarding any config changes 
to a multicast group. Each cluster node listens on the multicast group and 
applying the changes received within it's local configuration. This way it 
doesn't matter which node is the prime node. Any config received at any node 
will be automatically duplicated to any other node. 

## Configuration example

Within the vocs section of a configuration a cluster section must be added 
with the socket configuration of the cluster. This cluster socket must be 
used in any other configuration of the cluster too. 

Any changes will be automatically distributed via this cluster address.

{
	...
	"vocs" : {

		"cluster" : 
		{
			"host" : "224.0.0.1",
			"port" : 60000,
			"type" : "UDP"
		}
		...
	}
}

